<blockquote>
<p>Except it's a cicada, not a worm. And that personally, the picture reminds me more of wasps…! ;&gt;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Interestingly, in Chinese characters, the words for worm (蠕虫), cicada (蝉) and wasp (黄蜂) all have the 虫 radical (which is usually used for creeping animals and derived from logo-graphic models of a snake).</p>
<blockquote>
