<p>So, I'll be honest, this is the first version of this skip that I have read. That disclaimer out of the way, lets get in.</p>
<p>This article is alright. Not amazing, or terrible, but alright. For the first paragraph or so, I was really kind of trudging along, as it seemed to be typical &quot;parasite squick.&quot; However, the tie in with the Buddhism adds another dimension to this that really saves it from a downvote. I can totally buy into a group using these bugs in their religious practice.</p>
<p>If I was to nitpick anything, I would argue that the blackboxing of the site number doesn't really add any flavor and comes across more along the lines of blackboxing for the sake of blackboxing. Same with the recovery month and day.</p>
<p>In the end. +1</p>

